# The statistical surface: every path whose contents can move a number in
# parity/coverage_records.toml, and the facet each belongs to.
#
# A record stands until the surface it measured changes. It is attested while
# no path in a facet it depends on differs between the commit it was measured
# at (its calibration_sha) and HEAD; scripts/calibration_facets.py derives
# each record's facets from the record itself and computes the drift.
#
#   <facet> <path>     A path ending in "/" covers everything under it. A file
#                      belongs to the facet of the longest line that covers it.
#   core               Shared numerical and harness code. Every record
#                      carries it; a core edit owes remesure or a waiver.
#   estimator.*        One estimator implementation. A change invalidates
#                      only records whose `estimator` field matches.
#   identity.*         One identification path. A change invalidates only
#                      records whose query/estimator field matches.
#   other facets       A change invalidates only the records carrying the facet.
#   key <facet> <field> <pattern>...
#                      Records whose field matches a pattern carry the facet.
#   key_all <facet> <field>=<glob>[,<glob>...] <field>=<glob>...
#                      Every field clause must match; comma-separated patterns
#                      within one clause are alternatives. Separate rules remain OR.
#   allow <facet> <path> <name>...
#                      A reviewed reference from a file outside the facet to
#                      the facet's items, which cannot run the facet's code for
#                      records that do not carry it. Any other reference, and
#                      any stale name here, fails `calibration_facets.py check`.
#   testmod <path>     A reviewed file whose inline test-required modules use
#                      `#[cfg(test)]` or `#[cfg(all(test, feature="..."))]` and whose
#                      blocks hold unit-test scaffolding, not measurement (or that
#                      is itself a `#[cfg(test)] mod name;` file): an edit confined
#                      to them is not a change to the surface. No record's test or
#                      dgp may live in the file; `calibration_facets.py check`
#                      refuses one that does, and a suite file.
#
# Cargo.toml / Cargo.lock are compared with workspace version numbers removed:
# a release bump is not interval theory, but a feature, profile or external
# dependency change is.

# ---- estimator implementations (longer path wins over core src/) -----------
# Discovered-transport adapters have no execution path from fixed/catalog transport.
# Their current measured caller is the explicitly named DiscoveredTransport procedure.
# PCMCI+ also supplies JPCMCI+/RPCMCI and orientation-stability helpers; their
# eventual measurement identities must name these algorithms, never borrow PC/PCMCI evidence.
# The shared selective/contract.rs remains core: static PC also executes that file.
# Reviewed migration: current derived tags may be added to frozen70a71dd33 records;
# collector --retag retains their numerical SHA and historical surface_list_blob.
# test_calibration_dependency_facets.py checks that migration and current callers.
estimator.discovered_transport crates/antecedent/src/analysis/discovered_transport_estimate.rs
estimator.discovered_transport crates/antecedent/src/analysis/discovered_transport_temporal.rs
key estimator.discovered_transport query DiscoveredTransport
# Catalog search and exact transport plans are not used by regression/response
# constructors. The transport tests below replay the genuine changed paths;
# their unrelated records do not acquire a fabricated execution dependency.
# Selection separation serves ordinary/catalog/Z/meta/conditional transport and
# the SID-backed observation-recovery proof. Regression/discovery effect fits
# never call it. Keep recovery and proof consumers, including non-Transport keys.
identity.transport_selection crates/antecedent-identify/src/selection_separation.rs
key identity.transport_selection query *Transport* *Recovery* RecoveredEffect* Observation* CounterfactualEventQuery *MixedSource*
key identity.transport_selection estimator *transport* *recovery* *recovered*
key identity.transport_selection functional *transport* *recovery* *recovered*
